<title>USA: MoneyGram Payment Systems sets IPO terms.</title>
<headline>MoneyGram Payment Systems sets IPO terms.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>MoneyGram Payment Systems Inc plans to offer 14,463,750 shares at an estimated price of $15 to $17 each, according to a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>Of the total, 11,571,000 shares are being offered in the United States and Canada, and 2,892,750 in other countries.</p>
<p>The company, a non-bank provider of consumer money wire-transfer services, is set to make its debut on the New York Stock Exchange during the week of November 18, said underwriter Morgan Stanley.</p>
<p>The shares are being sold by Integrated Payment Systems Inc, a unit of First Data Corp.</p>
<p>---New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
